Boto3 is the AWS SDK(Software Development Kit) for Python.
It lets Python programs interact with AWS services programmatically.

For example, instead of manually creating an S3 bucket in the AWS Console:

import boto3
s3 = boto3.client("s3")
s3.create_bucket(
    Bucket="my-demo-bucket-12345"
)


Your Python code sends an API request to AWS.
Think of the flow as:

Python program
     ↓
    Boto3
     ↓
AWS API
     ↓
AWS Service
     ↓
S3 / EC2 / DynamoDB / Lambda / IAM / SQS / etc.
